    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Team SAAB, a design team consisting of  3 students from Stanford University and 4 from Linkoping University, Sweden were handed the challenge of improving aspects of the disaster space through technology by our partner SAAB. We designed a shelter that involves delivery via drone, whereupon they are assembled by the local population. The shelter consists of weather resistant tarp with reinforcing woven glass impregnated with moisture-hardening polyurethane. This system allows for modularity i.e. the shelter can be broken down into panels which allows for multiple modules to connect together using industrial-grade velcro. This system would help a large number of users stay together with their family in a safe, rigid and private home during the period where their homes are being rebuilt, which can be 5 years or more.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Berger, Brett; Zhang, Jiawei; Sridhar, Rajeev; Oesterbeck, Stephan; Schelling, Florence; Sorri, Philip; Stenberg, Jonathan; and Bengtsson, Marie. (2018). RESCUE HOME. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/gz384sy3895",
